NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.A has 16 observations and 2 variables.

5672       ;
5673       proc hpnlmod data=a out=b;
5674       parms alpha=.45 beta=.05 gamma=-.0025;
5675       x0 = -.5*beta / gamma;
5676       if (x < x0) then
5677       yp = alpha + beta*x + gamma *x*x;
5678       else
5679       yp = alpha + beta*x0 + gamma*x0*x0;
5680       model y ~ residual(yp);
5681       estimate 'join point' -beta/2/gamma;
5682       estimate 'plateau value c' alpha - beta**2/(4*gamma);
5683       predict 'predicted' yp pred=yp;
5684       predict 'response' y pred=y;
5685       predict 'x' x pred=x;
5686       run;


NOTE: The HPNLMOD procedure is executing in single-machine mode.
